  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Sportsman’s Warehouse returned to positive comparable-store sales, lifted by strong hunting, shooting and fishing demand, successful promotional events, and e-commerce gains. The consumer backdrop remains pressured by affordability and fuel costs, and a product-mix shift toward lower-margin categories compressed profitability. Intense competition from larger, well-capitalized sporting-goods chains continues to raise doubts about the durability of the niche recovery.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a turnaround that prioritizes profitability over expansion: closing underperforming stores, refraining from new openings, and aggressively reducing inventory and debt while investing in technology and loyalty upgrades to reinforce the core. Reaffirmed full-year guidance signals confidence in cost discipline, yet the market remains skeptical, as persistent net losses and margin erosion leave limited room for error against better-resourced rivals.",
